### Lab 5 - scenariusz audit logu (VS Code REST Client)
### Wymaga: docker compose up --build  oraz  docker compose exec api npx knex seed:run
@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Logowanie USER
# @name loginUser
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "mateusz.kalinski@example.com", "password": "Haslo-Testowe-2026" }

###
@userToken = {{loginUser.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Logowanie ADMIN
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "Admin-Haslo-2026" }

###
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Utworzenie rezerwacji (USER) -> 201 + event reservation.created
# @name created
POST {{base}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomId": 3, "participants": 10, "startTime": "2030-06-01T10:00:00Z", "endTime": "2030-06-01T11:00:00Z" }

###
@reservationId = {{created.response.body.id}}

### 4. Nieudana próba kolizji -> 409 ROOM_ALREADY_BOOKED, BRAK eventu
POST {{base}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomId": 3, "participants": 5, "startTime": "2030-06-01T10:30:00Z", "endTime": "2030-06-01T11:30:00Z" }

### 5. Anulowanie przez ADMINa -> 200 + event reservation.cancelled + [notification] w logach api
PATCH {{base}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Ponowne anulowanie -> 200 (idempotentne), BRAK eventu
PATCH {{base}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Audit log (ADMIN) - od najnowszych
GET {{base}}/api/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8. Audit log z filtrem
GET {{base}}/api/admin/audit-log?eventType=reservation.created&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9. Audit log jako USER -> 403
GET {{base}}/api/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
